_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d17\"},\"ref\":\"d17\",\"snippet\":\" ... Masjid in Delhi and dedicated it to its people. It continued to be the biggest mosque in India for over 300 years till the time Taj ul Masajid (or Tajul Masajid) in Bhopal claimed that spot in the early 1970s. So presenting to you the amazing Taj-ul ... \",\"title\":\"https://lemonicks.com/asia/india/madhya-pradesh/bhopal/complete-guide-taj-ul-masajid-the-largest-mosque-in-india/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d16\"},\"ref\":\"d16\",\"snippet\":\" ... yes\\n\\nThe Taj-ul-Masajid (), also known as the Tāj-ul-Masjid (), is a Sunni mosque, affiliated with Tablighi Jamaat, part of the Deobandi movement, located in Bhopal, in the state of Madhya Pradesh, India. With capacity for worshippers, it is the largest mosque in India and, , was ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taj-ul-Masajid\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e1\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d8\"},\"ref\":\"d8\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2 | 68,062 | Astana | | 2022 | |\\n| Istiqlal Mosque | 150px|center | | 93,200 | Jakarta | | 1978 | |\\n| Taj-ul-Masajid | 150px|center | | 23,000 | Bhopal | | 1901 | |\\n| Jamkaran Mosque | 150px|center | | 370,000 | Qom | | | |\\n| Egypt's Islamic Cultural Center (Masjid Misr Al Kabeer) | | 130,000 | 250,000 | New Administrative Capital | | 2023 | Sunni |\\n| Djamaa ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_largest_mosques\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"48a6db8ac12959d012ca7fcdcb09f2f9de3ec355083a24ca324aee8f50f700e7\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"4500d6150969aba62de9810895d31c4ce076861752a05a7540fa04e3b907fef1\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Taj-ul-Masajid Bhopal Moti Masjid Hamidia Hospital\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_15bbd7d71f0349329fee2031"},{"content":"I have strong evidence for the core criteria. The wikimapia snippet for Taj-ul-Masajid (d19) mentions \"Govt Hamidia Hospital and Gandhi Medical College 0...\" nearby, and Moti Masjid is 1.2 km away. Let me read the Wikipedia article on Taj-ul-Masajid to confirm the completion date, and read the wikimapia page to confirm the nearby hospital and mosque distances.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d16\"}","name":"read"},"id":"call_1e36b78f594a4e3aa61347f0","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d19\"}","name":"read"},"id":"call_910a877356894a55bd53a080","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d16\",\"document_chars\":4422,\"end\":3000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e3\",\"sha256\":\"cbd8bfa2e9ea977a4f4cad5a55d7bf1c5ec416b60a8e90a2d6ad70ab52acc9dc\",\"snapshot\":\"9a1abaf845a1fc844860ab223e44e8a2f5277aaba691e9ef2712a18e2c74bfe2\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: Taj-ul-Masajid - Wikipedia\\ndate: 2007-03-12\\n---\\nbuilding_name: Taj-ul-Masajid\\nimage_upright: 1.4\\nmap_type: India Madhya Pradesh\\nmap_size: 250\\nmap_relief: 1\\nmap_caption: Location of the mosque and dargah in Madhya Pradesh\\nlocation: Bhopal, Madhya Pradesh\\ncountry: India\\ncoordinates: 23.263 77.393 region:IN-MP dms inline, title\\nreligious_affiliation: Sunni Islam\\nrite: Deobandi movement(Tablighi Jamaat)\\nstatus: Mosque\\nfunctional_status: Active\\nwebsite: darululoomtajulmasajid.in\\narchitecture_type: Mosque architecture\\narchitecture_style: Indo-Islamic, Mughal\\nfunded_by: |}}\\nestablished: }}\\ngroundbreaking: 1887\\nyear_completed: 1958\\ncapacity: 175, 000 worshippers\\ninterior_area: 23000 m2\\ndome_quantity: Three\\nminaret_quantity: Two\\nminaret_height: 67\\n\\nembed: yes\\n\\nThe Taj-ul-Masajid (), also known as the Tāj-ul-Masjid (), is a Sunni mosque, affiliated with Tablighi Jamaat, part of the Deobandi movement, located in Bhopal, in the state of Madhya Pradesh, India. With capacity for worshippers, it is the largest mosque in India and, , was the ninth largest mosque in the world.\\n\\nHistory\\n\\nThe construction of the Taj-ul-Masajid was started by Nawab Shah Jahan Begum of Bhopal, in the newly built walled suburb of Shahjahanabad. The exact year when construction was started is unclear; Sharma estimated it to be 1871. The Bhopal-based journalist and the author of Masajid-e-Bhopal (), Aarif Aziz stated the date as 1887.\\n\\nAfter Shah Jahan Begum died in 1901, the mosque continued to be built by her daughter, Sultan Jahan Begum, till the end of her lifetime. The structure was planned in the midst of three water bodies, namely: Munshi Hussain Talab; Noor Mahal Talab; and Motia Talab. Hamidullah Khan helped construct one gate of the mosque on the suggestions of Shah Jahan Begum.\\n\\nThe construction work was later on led by Islamic scholar Imran Khan Nadwi, whose brother Salman Khan Nadwi, supervised the constructions. The construction was complete by 1958 at an expenditure of 20 million Indian rupees. The entrance of the mosque was renovated with motifs from 13th century Syrian mosques donated by the Emir of Kuwait in memory of his late wife.\\n\\nDuring the COVID-19 pandemic, the mosque was used as a vaccination center.\\n\\nArchitecture\\n\\nThe Taj-ul-Masajid largely takes inspiration from Mughal architecture. The mosque has a pink facade topped by two 18-storey high octagonal minarets with marble domes, an impressive main hallway with attractive pillars, and marble flooring resembling the likes of Jama Masjid in Delhi and the Badshahi Mosque of Lahore. It has a courtyard with a large ablution tank in the centre. It has a double-storeyed gateway with four recessed archways and nine cusped multifold openings in the main prayer hall. The massive pillars in the hall hold 27 ceilings through squinted arches of which 16 ceilings are decorated with ornate petalled designs.\\n\\nThe mosque also features a zenana, rare given that prayer from home was the norm for women at the time of the \"},\"executed\":true,\"next_start\":3000,\"ok\":true,\"previously_received\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_1e36b78f594a4e3aa61347f0"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d19\",\"document_chars\":1059,\"end\":1059,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e4\",\"sha256\":\"f11bcf812eb353d0c53bd36baeb1834eb615a818af0a0263328f5a7185a638f3\",\"snapshot\":\"f11bcf812eb353d0c53bd36baeb1834eb615a818af0a0263328f5a7185a638f3\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: Taj-ul-Masajid (Bhopal)\\n---\\nTaj-ul-Masajid (Bhopal)\\n\\nIndia /\\n\\nMadhya Pradesh /\\n\\nBhopal /\\n\\nMotia Talab\\n\\nWorld\\n\\n/ India\\n\\n/ Madhya Pradesh\\n\\n/ Bhopal\\n\\nWorld / India / Madhya Pradesh / Bhopal\\n\\nMosque and adjacent motia lake in the north, and mosque's extension in the south. This is the biggest Mosque in India and one of the biggest mosques in the World.\\n\\nNearby cities:\\n\\nCoordinates: 23°15'48\\\"N 77°23'30\\\"E\\n\\n- tajul masajid parking and ground 0.1 km\\n\\n- Darul Kaza ( ex Alexandria School) 0.1 km\\n\\n- mishra tent house 0.3 km\\n\\n- Benazir Ground 0.3 km\\n\\n- payga 0.4 km\\n\\n- kali basti 0.5 km\\n\\n- ALL SAINT S' SCHOOL 0.5 km\\n\\n- Pari Bazar 0.5 km\\n\\n- MARGHATIYA MANDIR 0.6 km\\n\\n- Islami Gate Ground 1 km\\n\\n- Moti talab 0.2 km\\n\\n- Noor Mahal Lake 0.3 km\\n\\n- Munshi Husain Khan ka Talab 0.4 km\\n\\n- Baab-e-Aali Cricket Stadium, Shahjehanadbad, Bhopal. 0.4 km\\n\\n- Taj Mahal, Bhopal 0.4 km\\n\\n- Govt Hamidia Hospital and Gandhi Medical College 0.5 km\\n\\n- Saifia College Campus 0.7 km\\n\\n- Bada Baagh Qabristan 0.7 km\\n\\n- Eidgaah Hills 1.4 km\\n\\n- Bhojtal/Bada Talaab 6.2 km\\n\\nComments\"},\"executed\":true,\"next_start\":null,\"ok\":true,\"previously_received\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_910a877356894a55bd53a080"},{"content":"Current control state (data, not source evidence):\n{\"current_notes_not_evidence\":[],\"evidence_shelf\":{\"omitted_for_capacity\":[],\"restored_exact_windows\":[],\"selection\":\"bounded recent first-delivery order; not a relevance/verification judgment\"},\"feedback\":null,\"instruction\":\"Read only useful passages. Notes and all-page cleanup are optional.\",\"literal_answer_contract\":{\"origin\":\"explicit experiment configuration, not inferred from question\",\"prefix\":\"\",\"suffix\":\"\"},\"phase\":\"RESEARCH\",\"remaining\":{\"action_slots\":194,\"backend_calls\":110,\"model_calls\":12,\"output_reservation\":47552},\"research_workflow\":{\"active_gap_not_verified\":null,\"available_pages_not_ranked_for_relevance\":[{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d20\"},\"ref\":\"d20\",\"snippet\":\" ... Bhopal\\n\\nWorld / India / Madhya Pradesh / Bhopal\\n\\npark, mosque\\n\\nSikander Jahan Begum of Bhopal during her rule built the Moti Masjid (meaning the Pearl Mosq\",\"title\":\"https://wikimapia.org/524502/Moti-Masjid-the-Pearl-Mosque\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":1059,\"ref\":\"e4\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d19\"},\"ref\":\"d19\",\"snippet\":\" ... Islami Gate Ground 1 km\\n\\n- Moti talab 0.2 km\\n\\n- Noor Mahal Lake 0.3 km\\n\\n- Munshi Husain Khan ka Talab 0.4 km\\n\\n- Baab-e-Aali Cricket Stadium, Shahjehanadbad\",\"title\":\"https://wikimapia.org/506522/Taj-ul-Masajid\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d18\"},\"ref\":\"d18\",\"snippet\":\" ... File:Upper Lake & VIP Road, Bhopal.JPG|A view of the upper lake\\nFile:Taj Mahal Bhopal.jpg | Taj Mahal main entrance bac